\"claim_id\": \"A-002\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"mission planners directed the veteran spacecraft to Uranus\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The spacecraft is Voyager 2, established in preceding sentence, not Voyager 3.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-003\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a journey that would take about 4,5 years\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact duration for the journey to Uranus.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-004\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"In fact, its encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference refers to Voyager 2's Jupiter encounter, not Voyager 3's.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-005\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The Uranus encounter's geometry was also defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Saturn\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states that Uranus encounter geometry was defined by Saturn encounter possibility.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-006\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim about Voyager 1's close study period.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-007\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Voyager 2 became the first human-made object to fly past Uranus\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference identifies Voyager 2, not Voyager 1, as the first human-made object to fly past Uranus.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-008\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Voyager 2 became the first human-made object to fly past Uranus, with short-range observations of the planet beginning January 24, 1986\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference specifies Voyager 2 and January 24, 1986, contradicting the claim's Voyager 1 and Jan. 31, 1987.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"when signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim about signal travel time.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Light conditions were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim about light conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED January 24, 1986\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference states the year as 1986, not 1968 as claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"at a range of about 81,500 kilometers (50,640 miles)\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference states 81,500 kilometers and 50,640 miles; the claim reverses these units.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-001\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Voyager 2 discovered 11 new moons\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-002\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"given such names as Pucka, Portila, Juliette, Kressida, Rosalinde, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelina, Ophelia, and Bianca II\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly lists these exact moon names.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-003\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"continuing a naming tradition begun in 1687\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim about the naming tradition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-004\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"three new rings in addition to the \\\"older\\\" eight rings\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim about the rings discovered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-005\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a magnetic field tilted at 66 degrees off-axis and off-center\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim about Uranus' magnetic field.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-006\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The spacecraft found wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere as high as 450 km/h (72400 meters per hour)\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states these exact wind speeds; the spacecraft is Voyager 2 from context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-007\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"found evidence of a boiling lake of water some 479 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim about the water lake evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-008\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Its rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this about Uranus' rings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Voyager 2 also returned spectacular photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariele, Umbrella, and Titan, five of Uranus' smaller moons\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim about the photos returned.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"In flying by Miranda at a range of only 17,560 miles (28,260 kilometers), the spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly century-long travels\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference states these same values with the spacecraft as Voyager 2; thousand-separator notation difference does not change the numerical values.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the tragic Challenger accident that killed six astronauts during their space shuttle launch\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference directly states this exact claim about the Challenger accident.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-013\",\n      \"verdict\": \"CONTRADICTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"on January 28, 1986\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference states January 28, 1986, not Feb. 28, 1986 as claimed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":26124,"type":"result","duration_ms":37992,"uuid":"5840f6cb-9d34-4839-b795-1e23aa2e6d6c","ttft_stream_ms":983,"time_to_request_ms":112,"first_content_frame_ms":984,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
